+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`TaskList.add` already validates title, priority and tags, rejects duplicates and returns a `Result`; rejected adds change nothing (see `task-input-validation`). Domain code must not throw nor read the clock or randomness.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Reuse `list.add` so import follows exactly the same rules as adding one task.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Quoting or escaping `;`, header rows, other delimiters, all-or-nothing import, or updating existing tasks.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Put the parser in `src/domain/import.ts` (pure, no throwing) and re-export from `src/index.ts`. It takes a `TaskList`, so the clock stays injected by the list.
+- Split text on `/\r?\n/`; number lines from 1 over every line; skip lines that are blank after trimming.
+- Split a line on `;`: more than 3 fields is rejected (`invalid-input`). Priority is trimmed; empty means omitted. Tags are split on whitespace, empty pieces dropped.
+- Validation is delegated to `list.add`; its error message becomes `reason`. Alternative of pre-validating was rejected as duplicating rules.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Partial import on mixed input → the report lists every rejected line so the user can fix and re-import only those.
+- Priority is case-sensitive like `add` (`High` is rejected) → consistent with existing behavior.
